course: dictionary
lesson: 14707
title: Probationary: on trial
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Probationary comes from probation, which means a trial: a test period to see if someone is good enough. «Mia has a probationary period of three months at her new job.» The clue is the trial. At the end, the boss decides whether she can stay for good.
explain: A «probationary teacher» is new and still being checked. They are not yet made permanent, which means the job is not yet theirs for always. Ask: what word would fit here? Try "on trial" in the sentence: "Mia has an on-trial period of three months" still makes sense, so probationary means on trial.
explain: In law, probationary is linked to probation. Someone who broke the law may be watched instead of sent to prison. «He has a probationary licence» tells you that his permission to drive is on trial, with checks. It is the same idea in a different place.
fact: Probationary means done or given for a trial time.
fact: «Probationary» means on trial, to check someone is good enough before they are made permanent.
fact: In law, «probationary» is linked to probation, when a person who broke the law is watched instead of sent to prison.
fact: A «probationary period» is a trial time, often a few months, at a new job.
fact: A good check is to swap in "on trial" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Sam is on a probationary period at his new job.» What does probationary mean? | Very happy and relaxed | Finished and permanent | *On trial, to see if he is good enough | Far away from home
exercise: «She is a probationary teacher this year.» What does this tell you? | She has never been to school | *She is new and still being checked | She is the head teacher | She has taught for twenty years
exercise: The new worker's job is ___ for three months, then the boss decides. Which word fits? | luminous | ancient | *probationary | curt
test: «He was given a probationary licence after the court case.» What does probationary suggest here? | *His licence is on trial, with checks | He lost his licence forever | He is a famous driver | His licence is for life
test: Which phrase means a new teacher who is still being checked? | retired teacher | head teacher | *probationary teacher | famous teacher
exam: Maya says probationary means "permanent". Is she right? Why or why not? | No, it means a kind of food | *No, it means on trial, the opposite of permanent | Yes, it means for always | Yes, it means very loud
